@rekram1-node lemme know if you are up for a discussion on this. 
Opencode desktop app is secretly hiding a powerful feature that products like superset.sh are actually asking folks to pay

It can already understand a worktrees, the only thing you need to do is make the chat window fully collapsible and the terminal expandable.

@thdxr I noticed that 55315bdffaae45d8a983b90836308ad460fc45e4 removed the `'return true'`
which made --agent stop working regardless of OPENCODE_FAST_BOOT, but the bug that I reported here is still not fixed:

If you set OPENCODE_FAST_BOOT=1 and use `--agent` then you still get the same error.

I don't think this bug is addressed and should be reopened.

If `OPENCODE_FAST_BOOT=1` then `ready` is still immediately `true`, with as a result that the TUI is started up (mounted) too early, calling `local.agent.set(args.agent)` while `sync.data.agent === []` still, which causes the toast (and rejection of the --agent) because `packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/context/local.tsx:111' :
```
          if (!agents().some((x) => x.name === name))
            return toast.show({
              variant: "warning",
              message: `Agent not found: ${name}`,
              duration: 3000,
            })
```
